WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.360
[Slow pace] [Thoughtful] Rusty opens his eyes.

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:13.699
[Short pause] He lies on a folded burlap sack next to an overturned wooden basket in the barn.

3
00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:25.167
[Slow pace] He pushes his big white paws against the rough jute fibers and presses his whiskers into a frayed seam.

4
00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.423
[Medium pause] [Thoughtful] He smells the fabric.

5
00:00:27.423 --> 00:00:32.390
[Short pause] He loves the smell.

6
00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.390
[Long pause]

7
00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:38.742
[Slow pace] Pipkin walks in, [Short pause] and says hello to Rusty.

8
00:00:38.742 --> 00:00:49.000
[Medium pause] [Curiosity] He sees a loose kernel of yellow feed-corn roll across the floor.

9
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.000
[Slow pace] [Cautious] He lowers his forehead to the stones and sniffs the tough corn kernel.

10
00:00:49.016 --> 00:00:50.016
[Long pause] [Thoughtful] He decides not to eat it; [Short pause] it smells old.

11
00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.030
[Slow pace] Rusty rolls onto his belly and gets up on all fours.

12
00:00:49.046 --> 00:00:50.046
[Medium pause] His long copper ears slap gently against his loose neck folds.

13
00:00:49.076 --> 00:00:50.076
[Slow pace] [Cautious] He steps onto the cold limestone slabs of the central barn aisle and presses his paws against the smooth gray stone.

14
00:00:49.087 --> 00:00:50.087
[Short pause] [Thoughtful] He feels the cool surface.

15
00:00:49.093 --> 00:00:50.093
[Short pause] It is slippery.

16
00:00:49.096 --> 00:00:50.096
[Long pause]

17
00:00:49.108 --> 00:00:50.108
[Slow pace] He trots to the strong base of the grain scale.

18
00:00:49.124 --> 00:00:50.124
[Medium pause] He lifts his left back leg to scratch behind his folded ear.

19
00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:50.148
[Slow pace] [Interest] Rusty lowers his heavy nose and tracks a line of crushed oat-husks along the stone seam.

20
00:00:49.162 --> 00:00:50.162
[Short pause] He walks the dry trail past the wooden harness-pegs.

21
00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:50.174
[Slow pace] Pipkin clamps his teeth on a dry wheat straw.

22
00:00:49.191 --> 00:00:50.191
[Short pause] He shakes his head twice and drops the broken stalk on the ground.

23
00:00:49.194 --> 00:00:50.194
[Long pause]

24
00:00:49.207 --> 00:00:50.207
[Slow pace] They go through the big double doors of the barn.

25
00:00:49.225 --> 00:00:50.225
[Medium pause] Pipkin pauses with his front paws resting on the raised iron door track.

26
00:00:49.242 --> 00:00:50.242
[Slow pace] [Curiosity] His upright left ear twitches toward the open farm yard.

27
00:00:49.273 --> 00:00:50.273
[Short pause] [Thoughtful] Down the dirt lane, [Short pause] the wooden chicken run stands quiet next to the cedar posts of the apple packing shed.

28
00:00:49.276 --> 00:00:50.276
[Long pause]

29
00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:50.289
[Slow pace] [Cautious] Rusty steps over the iron door-track.

30
00:00:49.312 --> 00:00:50.312
[Short pause] He walks onto the packed clay lane, lowers his head, and pushes his whiskers into the red dirt.

31
00:00:49.326 --> 00:00:50.326
[Slow pace] [Thoughtful] He tests the slope and feels the gravel.

32
00:00:49.351 --> 00:00:50.351
[Medium pause] Pipkin trots down the wooden ramp into the lane as the two puppies walk together to the open lower fields.

33
00:00:49.354 --> 00:00:50.354
[Long pause]

34
00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:50.375
[Slow pace] [Whisper] A dry wind blows over the tall fescue grass at the edge of the lower fields.

35
00:00:49.397 --> 00:00:50.397
[Medium pause] [Curiosity] A steady whistling sound comes from a drainage ditch next to the dry stone wall.

36
00:00:49.413 --> 00:00:50.413
[Slow pace] The vibration makes a hollow ring inside a hidden metal tube.

37
00:00:49.428 --> 00:00:50.428
[Short pause] [Cautious] Rusty stops walking and lowers his copper snout.

38
00:00:49.431 --> 00:00:50.431
[Long pause]

39
00:00:49.447 --> 00:00:50.447
[Slow pace] [Interest] Pipkin darts toward the ditch bank, his tail held high.

40
00:00:49.469 --> 00:00:50.469
[Medium pause] At the base of the dry stone wall, [Short pause] an angled corrugated iron pipe sits.

41
00:00:49.492 --> 00:00:50.492
[Slow pace] [Thoughtful] The metal cylinder channels water from the pasture when it rains heavily in autumn.

42
00:00:49.525 --> 00:00:50.525
[Long pause] [Surprised] Inside the lower opening, [Short pause] they see an old green rubber ball, [Short pause] wedged between two raised corrugation ridges.

43
00:00:49.547 --> 00:00:50.547
[Slow pace] [Interest] The rubber ball has fine surface cracks and has faded green from the summer sun.

44
00:00:49.558 --> 00:00:50.558
[Short pause] Pipkin drops low on his front elbows.

45
00:00:49.584 --> 00:00:50.584
[Slow pace] He stares directly into the iron pipe, [Short pause] where the round ball sits four inches past the metal lip.

46
00:00:49.598 --> 00:00:50.598
[Medium pause] [Whisper] Pipkin really wants that round green ball.

47
00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:50.601
[Long pause]

48
00:00:49.618 --> 00:00:50.618
[Slow pace] [Cautious] Rusty walks down the pasture slope with slow, careful steps.

49
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:50.633
[Short pause] His loose neck folds softly over his broad shoulders.

50
00:00:49.654 --> 00:00:50.654
[Slow pace] [Thoughtful] He lowers his head and puts his front pads on a flat fieldstone by the ditch.

51
00:00:49.674 --> 00:00:50.674
[Medium pause] His soft copper ears touch the wet stems of the chickweed and wild field-clover.

52
00:00:49.677 --> 00:00:50.677
[Long pause]

53
00:00:49.694 --> 00:00:50.694
[Slow pace] [Frustration] Pipkin snaps his jaws at the empty air above the pipe.

54
00:00:49.711 --> 00:00:50.711
[Short pause] He presses his scratchy whiskers right against the cold metal edge.

55
00:00:49.738 --> 00:00:50.738
[Slow pace] [Thoughtful] The ball stays perfectly still, [Short pause] tight against a seam where two pipe sections connect.

56
00:00:49.755 --> 00:00:50.755
[Medium pause] [Snorts] Pipkin snorts once and taps the iron with his front claws.

57
00:00:49.779 --> 00:00:50.779
[Slow pace] [Curiosity] Rusty pushes his black nose into the gap under the pipe to check the angle of the incline.

58
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.800
[Long pause] [Thoughtful] The iron cylinder rises at a steady slope toward the edge of the woods.

59
00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.816
[Slow pace] [Determination] Pipkin drops his chest flat on the ditch gravel.

60
00:00:49.835 --> 00:00:50.835
[Short pause] He pushes his firm, flat forehead right into the opening of the iron pipe.

61
00:00:49.852 --> 00:00:50.852
[Slow pace] He shoves with his back paws to drive his head into the dark channel.

62
00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:50.868
[Medium pause] His white whiskers scrape softly against the flaking metal.

63
00:00:49.887 --> 00:00:50.887
[Slow pace] [Determination] Pipkin strikes the faded green rubber ball with a powerful lunge!

64
00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:50.919
[Long pause] [Surprised] But now the ball slides deeper into the metal tube, [Short pause] fitting tightly between two raised ridges inside the pipe.

65
00:00:49.935 --> 00:00:50.935
[Slow pace] [Frustration] Pipkin digs his feet into the loose ditch gravel.

66
00:00:49.951 --> 00:00:50.951
[Short pause] His back paws spray red dirt across Rusty’s white front paws.

67
00:00:49.978 --> 00:00:50.978
[Slow pace] [Thoughtful] Pipkin pulls his head back out of the tube, his scruffy tan face smudged with black soot across his nose.

68
00:00:49.992 --> 00:00:50.992
[Medium pause] He sneezes twice into the dry grass of the pasture.

69
00:00:49.992 --> 00:00:51.992
[Long pause]
